  "scope": {
    "established": [
      "The 32-tile payload at ROM 0x080B9E94 is the BG2 tile set resident at VRAM 0x06002000 in the captured frames.",
      "The 32-byte payload at ROM 0x080B9F5C is palette bank 12, resident at PRAM 0x05000180 in the captured frames.",
      "The tile set is a fixed grid / highlight tile family: empty tiles, 1-pixel edge tiles and solid tiles with a 1-pixel border, in six colour families.",
      "The tile graphics and the palette are byte-identical across every captured frame of all four receipts; only the BG2 tilemap changes between states."
    ],
    "not_established": [
      "Which tilemap cells the game lights up: the BG2 tilemap content is generated at runtime and no ROM record for it was found.",
      "Whether the overlay marks reachable or unreachable ground: the layer is identified, its meaning is not.",
      "Whether the layer is reached by natural execution: the receipts are a scripted walk, not a coverage proof.",
      "Whether the 32 tiles are all used: the captured frames reference only part of the tile set.",
      "The screen-base unit convention (mGBA's block << 11 versus the 4 KB wording in common references) was not adjudicated in this round; the payload destination 0x06002000 is confirmed from the loader literal pool and from the VRAM dump independently of that convention.",
      "The PNG screenshots of the receipts are not self-consistent with their own dumps, so no pixel-level claim about the rendered overlay is made here."
    ]
  },
